# Captured resolution-order study — 2026-10-14, g++ 16, clang++ 22.1.8, Fedora (kernel 7.2.9-201.fc44.x86_64)
# Method: each candidate directory holds a distinct token marker (const char* sluice_f10_<dir>_marker) as liburing.h;
# the winner is whichever marker definition survives the preprocessor (-E) — 'system' means none did (the real header).
# Library traces: g++ -Wl,--trace on a TU referencing io_uring_queue_init; fakelib is 'cp -L /usr/lib64/liburing.so'.
# Every line below is captured stdout/stderr of the commands shown (marker dirs under /tmp/f10-study2 are ephemeral).

== g++ 16, which liburing.h a C++ compile of <liburing.h> opens ==
no env                        => system
C_INCLUDE_PATH=cinc           => system
CPATH=cpath                   => cpath
CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH=cplus      => cplus
CPATH + CPLUS                 => cpath
-I pin + CPATH + CPLUS        => pin
-I pin + CPATH, quote include => pin
clang++, -I pin + CPATH       => pin
CPATH only, clang++           => cpath

